## Methodology

Phase 3 proposes a tighter AUDIT-6 admission predicate:
  m3 >= 80 AND (fcbr >= 0.5 OR edge_density >= 0.45)

vs the Phase 1 predicate:
  m3 >= 80

The disjunction protects codec_wiki (admits via fcbr 0.904) and 1189261
(admits via edge_density 0.490) while excluding the 2 CLIC web photos
with m3 >= 80 (clic_22ea12 fcbr=0.278/ed=0.167, clic_0c49a5
fcbr=0.080/ed=0.336) that the AUDIT-7 wider-corpus bench surfaced.

## Key finding

The 4-cell bisect shows BYTE-IDENTICAL output to AUDIT-7 pre-Phase-3
baseline on every (image, effort, distance) — confirming that AUDIT-6
was NOT firing on the CLIC photos in production in the first place. The
outer W44-109 `is_screenshot = mask1x1_median > 95` gate excludes them
before the AUDIT-6 admission predicate is consulted. The CLIC SSIM2
wedge (clic_22ea12 e7 d=4 -3.84 SSIM2) has a SEPARATE root cause that
is orthogonal to AUDIT-6.

Phase 3 ships as DEFENSIVE NARROWING: structurally correct (cannot
enlarge the firing set), forward-compatible (kicks in if future
`is_screenshot` promotion brings CLIC photos into the W44-109 admission
class). Zero observable byte change today.

